%description:
The TR 38.901 rural macrocell path loss takes log10(h) of the average building height h: at h = 0 m
it is -inf, and the run went on with a non-finite path loss (a NaN SINR, no CQI). A building height
of 0 m or less is an error on the first evaluation of a link of the cell, whatever
tolerateHeightViolation says: no study range can make the formula defined there.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

# a rural macrocell (TR 38.901 RMa), whose path loss takes the building height and street width
*.gnb.cellularNic.radio.scenario = "RURAL_MACROCELL"
*.gnb.cellularNic.radio.buildingHeight = 0m
**.nrChannelModel[*].tolerateHeightViolation = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
the cell's building height is 0 m and its street width 20 m (the buildingHeight and streetWidth of its base station's radio), and the path loss of the scenario RURAL_MACROCELL takes their logarithms: both must be above 0 m
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
